  "notes": "GOLD v1 (gold fixer round 1, 2026-10-18) for sc_eaa89c6d1f1f (40500000_0_SCAN1 1.ply, part 40500000, tagged PARTIAL_SCAN_1 but every bend is formed (cad_crosscheck); CAD bend lines 9; CONSUMED in BENCHMARK_V3). Started from benchmark_v2/label_lines/sc_eaa89c6d1f1f/pairs.json and prep benchmark_v2/label_prep/sc_eaa89c6d1f1f. Part: open rectangular tray, t ~1.0-1.2 mm. Base 1/2 (~194 x 123 mm) with four ~43 mm walls folded up 90 deg: long walls 3/4 and 5/6, short walls 7/8 and 9/10. Each short-wall fold is interrupted by two ~29 mm ear windows, where the wall is notched and flat ears (with holes) continue the base plane outward; the ears are coplanar with the base and are not bends. The long-wall fold B2 crosses a ~13 mm semicircular base relief. The wall tops carry five inward 90 deg flanges/tabs: 11 (~48 mm, on short wall 9/10), recessed tabs 12 (long wall 3/4) and 14 (long wall 5/6), and corner tabs 13 and 15 (short wall 7/8, butting against the long walls). 9 formed bends = CAD 9; three auditors and the fixer's raw-point sections agree. The four vertical box corners are butt seams (wall end against wall face, no arc) and are not bends. Also not bends: hole and window walls, ears, thickness and perimeter edges, thin strip 16 (wall-end thickness face at the x-/y- corner), and the unscanned diamond in the base bottom skin (a scan gap, not an emboss). All lines are outer-skin apex (--locus apex). GOLD FIX: B3 and B4 (base to short walls) sat in air ~1.3 mm outside the outer arc, because in envelope mode the flat ear/base points inside the windows, which pass through the OML sharp, set the apex floor (apex offset -0.33/-0.38 mm). apex_mode station_median puts both on the outer-arc apex (offset 0.94/0.97 mm; raw-point fold stations within -0.05..+0.07 mm of the line). B8's start and B9's end are extended to the visible fold ends (coverage ~87% -> ~97%). B1, B2 and B5-B7 are unchanged (3/3 auditors OK).",
